License cheat sheet (three different things — do not mix them up)
-----------------------------------------------------------------

1. OUR CODE (this repo's Rust) → MIT-0. See LICENSE.

2. LOADER LIBRARIES (Candle, tokenizers, hf-hub) → Apache-2.0 OR MIT.
   This is the Rust *code* that reads GGUF files and runs inference.
   Apache applies to Candle/Hugging Face software — NOT to Meta or Google
   model weights.

3. MODEL WEIGHTS (the actual neural nets) → separate licenses:
   - Meta Llama 3.1 → Llama 3.1 Community License (NOT Apache)
   - Google Gemma 3, EmbeddingGemma → Gemma Terms of Use (NOT Apache)
     (Gemma 4 uses Apache 2.0; we use Gemma 3, which does not.)


When to say "Built with Llama"
------------------------------
Meta requires "Built with Llama" when you distribute or make available:
  (a) Llama Materials (weights or derivatives), OR
  (b) a product or service that contains Llama Materials.

This repo is a published harness built to run Llama 3.1 weights, so we
display "Built with Llama" in README (product documentation).

You do NOT say "Built with Llama" for Candle's Apache-licensed loader code
alone. That is a different license on different material.

Local-only use of Llama weights you already downloaded, with no
distribution, has lighter requirements — but this public repo still needs
the notices below because we distribute the harness and its docs.


